# Kconfig fragment: sched_ext, the BPF-loadable scheduler class (2026-11-15).
#
# Profile-scoped: listed in nvidiahard's PROF_LIVE_KFRAGS only, as an experiment
# on the nvhard host (~/Claude/info/plan-kernel-performance-20261114.md). The
# gaming distributions build it (CachyOS config; Bazzite and the Steam Deck ship
# the scx schedulers); the one published desktop test showed little on average
# FPS and its gain in the 1 % lows. Nothing is measured here yet: move it into
# performance.fragment for every hard profile only after a host A/B says so.
#
# With the option on and no BPF scheduler loaded the kernel schedules exactly as
# before (EEVDF); a scheduler is loaded by root from userspace (sys-kernel/scx:
# scx_lavd, scx_flash, scx_bpfland) and the kernel falls back to EEVDF when it
# exits or stalls. Loading needs CAP_BPF/root; BPF_UNPRIV_DEFAULT_OFF stays.
#
# Depends on BPF_SYSCALL && BPF_JIT && DEBUG_INFO_BTF && !SCHED_ALT: the first
# three come from live.fragment (BTF is kept alive there despite RANDSTRUCT, see
# its comment). If BTF is ever dropped by olddefconfig, this symbol goes with it
# silently, so a queue must check the final .config.
CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT=y

# The function tracer is what makes the schedulers loadable at all. Every scx
# scheduler also attaches fentry/tracing BPF programs, and a BPF trampoline is
# patched over the 5-byte NOP that only FUNCTION_TRACER (-mfentry) puts at each
# function entry. Without it the kernel finds other bytes there and refuses:
#   Error: Failed to attach non-struct_ops BPF programs ... Device or resource busy
# (__bpf_arch_text_poke -> -EBUSY; measured on nvhard 2026-11-16, kernel #10:
# every scx_* failed, and systemd's own LSM BPF program 'restrict_filesystems'
# fails the same way on every kernel built without it). sys-kernel/scx only
# checks ~FTRACE, which is not enough. DYNAMIC_FTRACE defaults to y with it and
# brings DYNAMIC_FTRACE_WITH_DIRECT_CALLS. Cost: ftrace's function hooks exist
# for root (tracefs); the NOPs themselves are free.
CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER=y
CONFIG_DYNAMIC_FTRACE=y
